{"profile":{"name":"Gord Perks","ward":"Ward 4, Parkdale—High Park","bio":"First elected to Toronto City Council in 2006 to represent Ward 14 Parkdale-High Park; has represented Ward 4 Parkdale-High Park since the 2018 ward amalgamation and was re-elected in 2022. Before council, he worked in the environmental movement from 1987 to 2005 with Pollution Probe, Greenpeace Canada, the Better Transportation Coalition and the Toronto Environmental Alliance; he is the principal author of the Canadian Green Consumer Guide, a former Eye Weekly environment columnist, and a former adjunct professor with the University of Toronto's Environmental Studies department. In April 2026 he announced he will not seek re-election at the end of the 2022-2026 term.","committees":["Planning and Housing Committee (Chair)","Budget Committee (Vice-Chair)","Civic Appointments Committee","Striking Committee","Executive Committee","Housing Rights Advisory Committee"],"contact":{"email":"councillor_perks@toronto.ca","phone":"416-392-7919"},"promises":[{"text":"Signed the Toronto Environmental Alliance's Greener City for All election pledge in 2022, committing to support priority actions including fully funding Toronto's climate strategy (2025/2030/2040 targets), overhauling heating and cooling bylaws and a fair stormwater charge for climate resilience, and regulations to eliminate unnecessary single-use items toward a zero-waste city.","source":"http://election.torontoenvironment.org/pledge_results"},{"text":"Signed the Toronto Alliance to End Homelessness's Pledge to End Homelessness in 2022, committing to make ending homelessness through housing solutions a top City priority in the coming term, set minimum housing access targets for people experiencing homelessness, increase financial resources through a dedicated fund, and develop a Toronto Ending Homelessness Plan.","source":"https://paul-bruce-o84i.squarespace.com/s/THHSP-Forum-Slide-Deck-November-16-2022.pdf"}]},"lobbying":{"total":943,"term":244,"first":"2010-08-24","last":"2026-10-08","lobbyists":268,"clients":204,"subjects":494,"methods":{"Meetings":354,"Emails":443,"Phone calls":35,"Written":77,"Other or unreported":34},"top":[{"label":"Economic Development","count":199},{"label":"By-law / Regulation","count":142},{"label":"Licences / Licensing","count":136},{"label":"Planning and Development Application, Zoning By-law","count":72},{"label":"Planning and Development","count":65}],"years":[{"year":2010,"count":4},{"year":2011,"count":36},{"year":2012,"count":46},{"year":2013,"count":74},{"year":2014,"count":62},{"year":2015,"count":72},{"year":2016,"count":60},{"year":2017,"count":47},{"year":2018,"count":47},{"year":2019,"count":89},{"year":2020,"count":23},{"year":2021,"count":38},{"year":2022,"count":36},{"year":2023,"count":73},{"year":2024,"count":82},{"year":2025,"count":56},{"year":2026,"count":20}],"undated":78,"snapshot":"2026-10-23"},"declaredInterests":[{"Declarant":"Gord Perks","VerbalDeclarationDate":"2017-01-17","Committee":"Toronto and East York Community Council","Item":"2017.TE21.41","ItemTitle":"Parking Amendments - Beaconsfield Avenue","VerbalDeclaration":"as he lives around the corner from this street.","Term":"2014-2018"},{"Declarant":"Gord Perks","VerbalDeclarationDate":"2015-11-10","Committee":"Toronto and East York Community Council","Item":"2015.TE12.107","ItemTitle":"Nomination of Beaconsfield Avenue for Heritage Conservation District Study","VerbalDeclaration":"in that his residence is immediately adjacent to the study area.","Term":"2014-2018"},{"Declarant":"Gord Perks","VerbalDeclarationDate":"2013-12-19","Committee":"City Council","Item":"2013.EX36.17","ItemTitle":"2014 Rate Supported Budgets - Toronto Water and 2014 Water and Wastewater Rates and Service Fees","VerbalDeclaration":"as his spouse works for an organization which received grants from the City.","Term":"2010-2014"},{"Declarant":"Gord Perks","VerbalDeclarationDate":"2013-02-28","Committee":"Toronto and East 